HOMO-LUMO gap; hence a negligible color change was observed (Figure S21).
To demonstrate the potential use of this EAS chemistry as a post-synthetic modification process,we examined the porosities of the resulting MOFs. Prior to acquiring the ${\sf N}_{2}$ adsorption and desorption isotherms, Soxhlet extraction was performed using methanol to remove the coordinated halides, $H_{3}O^{+}$ , and unreacted reagents. Interestingly， the adsorption-desorption isotherms reveal that the ${\sf N}_{2}$ uptake at $0.1~P/P_{0}$ for ${\mathsf{C o}}_{2}(5.$ -alkyl- $.m$ -DOBDC) prepared by EAS with an alkyl halide was lower than that of the pristine $\mathsf{C o}_{2}(m\mathrm{-}\mathsf{D O B D C})$ (Figure 4a). In contrast, the ${\sf N}_{2}$ uptake at $0.95~P/P_{0}$ was the same or higher, with significant hystereses observed in the adsorption-desorption isotherms (type H4 for $\mathsf{C o}_{2}(5\$ -methyl- $.m.$ -DOBDC)and ${\mathsf{C o}}_{2}(5.$ -ethyl- $.m.$ -DOBDC) and type H2(b) for $\mathsf{C o}_{2}(5\$ -propyl-m-DOBDC)) compared to that of pristine $\mathsf{C o}_{2}(m{\mathsf{\mathrm{-}}}\mathsf{D O B D C})$ (Figure 4a).[18] The appearance of the hysteresis, which was not observed for pristine $\mathsf{C o}_{2}$ (m-DOBDC) (Figure S22), indicates that the introduction of mesopores led to the formation of hierarchical micro- and mesoporous structures. According to nonlocal density functional theory (NLDFT), the calculated pore size distributions of $\mathsf{C o}_{2}$ (5-methyl- $.m$ -DOBDC) and $\mathsf{C o}_{2}(5\$ -ethyl-mDOBDC) are centered at $3.9\mathsf{n m}$ , while $\mathsf{C o}_{2}(5\$ -propyl- $m$ -DOBDC) exhibited two distinct types of mesopore, centered at $3.9\mathsf{n m}$ and $5.8\mathsf{n m}$ (Figures 4a and S23).
